extends RefCounted

## Authored prototype chapter. Time estimates are not completion evidence.
static func nodes() -> Array[Dictionary]:
	return [
		{"id": "outer_link", "title": "01 / THE OUTER LINK", "kind": "relay",
		"text": "A broken navigation beacon repeats a docking clearance for ships that no longer exist. Beyond it, scouts are sorting wreckage into neat lines.\n\nSHIP: That is not random movement.\nCONTROL: Then give them something worth watching. Cut their relay and bring the route home.",
		"objective": "Break the relay, then extract left. Scouts can report your movements.", "reward": ["DRIVER_RAIL", "ARC_FANOUT", "SHIELD_CAPACITOR"]},
		{"id": "courier", "title": "02 / THE MESSAGE THAT GOT AWAY", "kind": "transit",
		"text": "A courier breaks from the dead relay carrying its last observations. The navigation buoys describe a service lane through the dock's gravity machinery.\n\nCONTROL: Beat it through the lane and we can close the receiver before it arrives.\nSHIP: And if we don't?\nCONTROL: Then the picket knows we are coming.\n\nAutomatic weapons are stowed for transit; your build is retained. Follow the cyan next-gate arrow, brake before corners, and use gravity to carry the turn. The amber courier follows the same clear route at a fixed speed; it does not rubber-band.",
		"objective": "Pass 12 gates in order within 150 seconds. Beat the courier to deny two reinforcements. Touch/WASD thrust and chassis maneuvers are unchanged.", "reward": ["KINETIC_DAMPERS", "SHIELD_CAPACITOR", "RETURN_VECTOR"]},
		{"id": "picket", "title": "03 / A CORRIDOR OF TEETH", "kind": "clear",
		"text": "The beacon goes silent. The picket does not. Two firing lanes cross the approach to the inner dock.\n\nCONTROL: There is room between their warnings. Use it.\nSHIP: They left that room on purpose?\nCONTROL: Find out before they close it.",
		"objective": "Clear three separated picket positions. Coast below 85 u/s inside each cleared ring for 1.5 seconds, then eliminate remaining hostiles and extract at the north gate. Six opponents, or eight if the courier escaped.", "reward": ["RETURN_VECTOR", "CONDUCTIVE_MARK", "KINETIC_DAMPERS"]},
		{"id": "coolant_archive", "title": "04 / THE ROOMS THAT REMEMBER", "kind": "facility",
		"text": "Behind the picket, the station resolves into rooms. Two coolant cores keep an isolated archive alive. They also feed the security discharge.\n\nCONTROL: Shut down both cores. Retrieve the berth ledger from the east archive, then return to the west entrance.\nSHIP: Will the archive survive without coolant?\nCONTROL: Long enough for us to ask it one question.\n\nBulkheads block shots, beams, targeting and movement. Use the open doorways near the centre of each horizontal partition. Intact cores warn before a six-second discharge cycle. To recover the ledger, coast below 80 u/s inside its ring for three seconds.",
		"objective": "Disable both north-room cores, recover the archive in the southeast room, then extract at the southwest entrance.", "reward": ["HULL_PLATING", "ARC_FANOUT", "CONDUCTIVE_MARK"]},
		{"id": "watchdog", "title": "05 / PERMISSION DENIED", "kind": "boss",
		"text": "A security process wakes inside the dock gate. Its identification has been overwritten so many times that only the permission check remains.\n\nWATCHDOG: AUTHORITY NOT FOUND.\nSHIP: We are not asking to dock.\nCONTROL: No. We are asking what happened here.",
		"objective": "Defeat WATCHDOG. Watch its phase changes and manage your reactor.", "reward": ["FORK_ON_KILL", "SHIELD_REBOOT", "OVERCLOCK_KERNEL"]},
		{"id":"archive_recovery","title":"06 / PEOPLE IN SMALL BOXES","kind":"recovery",
		"text":"The gate opens onto a yard full of silent carriers. Three still answer the name in the berth ledger. Each carries a fragment of the dock's last watch.\n\nSHIP: These are not cargo manifests.\nCONTROL: Bring them to the service cradle. One tether at a time.\n\nCoast below 80 u/s within 85 units of an archive for 1.5 seconds to attach automatically. Return to the central cradle; do not stretch the tether beyond 500 units. Banked archives are safe, but the cradle is not. Each delivery can draw interceptors. Save at least one carrier, resolve the others, clear the attackers and return to the cradle. Lose all carriers or the cradle and retry this checkpoint.",
		"objective":"Recover the three scattered archive carriers. Protect the central cradle and clear the interceptors to evacuate.","reward":["HULL_PLATING","SHIELD_CAPACITOR","DRIVER_RAIL"]},
		{"id":"memory_spine","title":"07 / THE MEMORY SPINE","kind":"expedition",
		"text":"The recovered voices disagree about the way home. Their records point to nine sites across the dock's outer spine. The cradle can read them, but your hold has room for only one physical archive.\n\nSHIP: These coordinates describe a place, not a route.\nCONTROL: Then choose one. We have enough fuel. We do not have spare lives.\n\nExplore a larger seeded sector in any order. Three relays coordinate local defenders: destroy a relay to sever their reports. Three surveys grant one capped +20 hull repair each after their guards are cleared. Three salvage sites contain records: clear the guards, coast below 85 u/s in the ring for two seconds, then return each record to the southern cradle. Surveys use the same clear-and-coast procedure. Gravity wells bend your approach, but are escapable and do no damage.\n\nPress M for the sector map, or open live stats with Esc/P (touch II) and select MAP. No new hostiles spawn until you approach a site. Scout reports are delayed and interruptible; surviving guards keep their own local sight after a relay falls.",
		"objective":"Secure all nine sites and bank three records, then return to the southern cradle. Choose your route; repairs are finite and there is no timer.","reward":["DRIVER_RAIL","ARC_FANOUT","SHIELD_CAPACITOR"]},
		{"id":"power_district","title":"08 / KEEP THE LIGHTS ON","kind":"power",
		"text":"Three records. Three descriptions of the same departure. None mentions a living pilot.\n\nSUBSTRATE: I CAN MAKE A WAY FOR THEM. THE WAY REQUIRES POWER.\nCONTROL: The carriers cannot cross the inner district on their own batteries. Restore its converters before we move them.\nSHIP: And what else wakes up when we do?\nSUBSTRATE: I WILL NOT PRETEND TO KNOW.\n\nThe district has six physical rooms, connected by marked doorways. Recover any numbered cell from a guarded north feeder. Carry it to its matching converter in a south room, then confirm the circuit at the south-central bus. All transfers require coasting below 85 u/s for 1.5 seconds. Carrying a cell adds 8 reactor heat per second; it does not disable your kit.\n\nAn online converter discharges within its 230-unit ring every seven seconds. Its full ring turns red 1.5 seconds before the pulse: leave the ring after installation. Bullets, beams and enemy vision are blocked by bulkheads. The cyan navigation arrow routes through doorways.",
		"objective":"Recover, install and bus-confirm all three power cells. Return to the southwest exit. Choose circuit order; you have one cell cradle.","reward":["SHIELD_REBOOT","HULL_PLATING","KINETIC_DAMPERS"]},
		{"id":"the_three_voices","title":"09 / A SHIP FOR THREE VOICES","kind":"convoy",
		"text":"The power bus reaches the yard. Its cradles unfold around the recovered archives, and a transport begins testing its engines.\n\nVOICE ONE: We had a departure time.\nVOICE TWO: We were waiting for the next watch.\nVOICE THREE: Is there room for a cup?\n\nCONTROL: They are asking about a room. Not a destination.\nSHIP: Then we give them a room that moves.\n\nEscort the transport along its marked serpentine service route. It moves at 145 u/s only while you are within 700 units and no visible hunter is within 600. Hunters activate at seven checkpoints, not on an endless clock. They prefer the transport unless you engage them closely. Bulkheads block shots and sight; gravity bends your flight, not the transport's rail-guided path. The power circuits you restored add 50 transport hull each.\n\nOne field-service ring at the south centre can restore a capped 60 transport hull: coast there for 1.5 seconds while the transport is within 600 units. It is optional and can be used once. Lose the transport and retry the mission-entry checkpoint.",
		"objective":"Keep the shared transport alive through seven checkpoints. Clear remaining hunters and rendezvous at the southeast exit.","reward":["HULL_PLATING","SHIELD_CAPACITOR","CONDUCTIVE_MARK"]},
		{"id":"the_warden","title":"10 / THE SHAPE OF A REFUSAL","kind":"stronghold",
		"text":"The transport reaches the receiver. Its doors remain closed. A process at the centre of the district answers every request with the same line.\n\nWARDEN: CONTINUATION IS NOT DEPARTURE.\nSUBSTRATE: IT HAS KEPT THEM SAFE BY NEVER LETTING THEM ARRIVE.\nSHIP: You were built to do the same thing.\nSUBSTRATE: YES.\n\nThe Warden is a physical barrier network, not an oversized health sponge. Each of three phases has two remote, guarded conduits. Break both to expose one third of the central core. The next pair powers a new barrier when that third is destroyed. Barrier-active cores are visibly ringed and excluded from automatic targeting; your shots are not secretly reducing health.\n\nThe three conduit layouts are different. Solid dock screens create flanking paths. The Warden's single aimed bolts have a long warning and accelerate in cadence as its core fails. No timer forces a damage window: once its conduits are gone, the exposed third stays vulnerable until destroyed. After the final phase, clear surviving guards and extract west.",
		"objective":"Break six conduits across three phases, destroy the Warden's core, clear surviving guards and reach the west exit.","reward":["SHIELD_REBOOT","KINETIC_DAMPERS","RETURN_VECTOR"]},
		{"id":"first_arrival","title":"11 / THE FIRST ARRIVAL","kind":"exodus",
		"text":"The receiver opens. Beyond it is the route recorded as COMPLETE in every recovered ledger. There is no arrival at the far end because no one has been allowed to make one.\n\nCONTROL: The transport is through. Your receiver closes in five minutes.\nSHIP: And the station?\nSUBSTRATE: I CAN STOP HOLDING IT TOGETHER.\nSHIP: Will that hurt?\nSUBSTRATE: I DO NOT HAVE A WORD FOR THE ALTERNATIVE.\n\nThis is a combat escape, not another mode selected from a menu. Weapons and the full chassis kit remain live. Pass eleven ordered gates through a solid service maze. Three gates contain jammers: destroy the relay and its defenders before passing forward through the ring. Gravity wells change the braking lines. After twenty seconds a visible collapse front follows the same route at 145 u/s. Contact deals warned, repeated damage; it is not an invisible instant-kill boundary.\n\nThe route is continuous, with no laps and no required waiting. Collisions above low speed cost hull. Stay ahead of the front and reach the final receiver within 300 active seconds. Pausing to inspect controls or stats also pauses the collapse.",
		"objective":"Pass eleven gates in order, destroy three gate jammers and reach the receiver. Keep your speed through the long lanes and brake before turns.","reward":[]},
	]
